# Code Structure Rules

Canonical blueprint: `docs/guides/feature-folder-structure.md`.

## Feature folders

- Module code lives in `apps/edubridge/features/<module>/` with: `components/`, `hooks/`, `queries/`, `actions/`, `lib/`, `types.ts`, `index.ts`, `README.md`.
- Other code imports a module **only** via its `index.ts` public surface. Deep imports into another module are forbidden.
- Modules never import other modules. Shared needs go up: UI → `packages/ui`, DB schema → `packages/db`, helpers → `apps/edubridge/lib/`.
- Promote something to a shared package only when 2+ modules consume it.
- Route files in `apps/edubridge/app/` stay thin — compose feature exports only.

## Navigation

- All navigation is defined in the shell module registry (`features/shell/modules.ts`): `{ id, title, href, icon, allowedRoles }`. Staff uses `modules`; family uses `familyModules` (cookie Path `/family`). Never hard-code nav links elsewhere.
- Menu items for forbidden roles are filtered **server-side** — never sent to the client. Family chrome is `FamilyShell`, not staff `ShellLayout`.

## Boundaries

- AI logic lives only in `apps/agent` (Mastra workflows). The product app calls it through the typed client in `apps/edubridge/lib/` — never embeds LLM calls/prompts in the app.
- `apps/web` is the Mastra starter/demo only (port 3002) — do not add product modules there.
- `packages/ui` and `packages/ai-ui` contain **no school-domain logic** — domain-agnostic primitives only.
- ShadCN components are added via `pnpm ui:add <name>` at repo root (into `packages/ui`), never inside an app.

## Styling trigger

Before UI/visual work, read `docs/design/MASTER.md` (light-only system). Before changing Tailwind/ShadCN configuration, read `TAILWIND_SHADCN_GUIDE.md` — the two-compilation model (packages/ui + per-app) is deliberate. Component ladder: `docs/design/component-policy.md`.
